cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "hep-simkernels: Geant4-matched particle-matter kernels for fast simulation"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
authors:
  - family-names: Mina
    given-names: Rob
    affiliation: "University of Virginia"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2241-8566"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RobMina/hep-simkernels"
license: "Apache-2.0"
abstract: >-
  hep-simkernels re-implements named Geant4 11.3.2 electromagnetic models for fast simulation: muon energy loss with fluctuations, electron ionisation, multiple scattering, Seltzer-Berger bremsstrahlung, positron annihilation, muon radiative losses, slab propagation and straight-line transport through GDML geometry. Each kernel has a NumPy reference and, where it runs on a device, a JAX twin in float32 and float64; NIST materials and experiment hooks keep the package experiment-neutral. Compact copies of the Geant4 Seltzer-Berger and Mott data travel with it under the Geant4 Software License.
keywords:
  - "fast simulation"
  - "Geant4"
  - "energy loss"
  - "multiple scattering"
  - "bremsstrahlung"
  - "JAX"
  - "GPU"
  - "particle physics"
